# Example development configuration for the mobile platform.
# Copy this file to `.env.development` (or `.env`) and adjust the values for
# your machine. Vite picks the file by mode: `pnpm dev` runs in development
# mode and reads `.env.development` over `.env`; `pnpm build` uses production
# and `pnpm build:staging` staging. Never commit the real file.
#
# On a phone or emulator, localhost is the device itself: use your computer's
# LAN address (or 10.0.2.2 on the Android emulator) to reach a local API.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to import.meta.env — an
# unprefixed variable here would be silently invisible to the app.

# --- REST API ------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the Lpaecomms REST API, including the /api/v1 prefix.
# development: http://localhost:3000/api/v1
# staging:     https://staging.lpaecomms.example/api/v1
# production:  https://lpaecomms.example/api/v1
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
